body:
@lunny another incorrect behaviour found:

1. Assuming you have a primary branch named `base`, two different feature branches `f1` and `f2` and two independent PRs: `#8` from `f1` to `base` (4 files changed) and `#12` from `f2` to `base` (10 files changed);
2. Cherry-pick some changes from `f1` to `f2`, now `#12` contains 12 changed files;
3. Open `#12` and mark all files as viewed (and see correct mark: `12/12 files viewed`)
4. Merge `#8` to `base` branch
5. Open `#12` again and see incorrect result:
    <img width="582" height="849" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d57cb965-69ca-406a-a3d9-de21b8e17b8c" />
   In fact, after merge only original 10 files changed relative to updated `base` branch, but counter stored previous value `12` and we have 12/10.

In this situation refreshing the page don't fixes incorrect value.
